notes               = "Untitled in source. English block is a raw machine draft (kept in the machine section); finished translation pending. کوره‌راه is one word — a byway or narrow track — not کوره (kiln) + راه (road): the machine pass read it as 'the furnace of the roads' and the first lantern kept a trace of that as 'kiln-hot tracks'. Corrected to 'back roads', which is also how Farrokhi's quotation of this poem reads in the preface."
draft               = true

===persian===

در کوره راه ها....
آبی خاکستری سیاه
پیکر دهقانی است با چوبدست بلندش
سپید سیاه
خرش را میگویم
با خرواری از خارهای باران زده
سیاه سیاه
بختش را میگویم
که همچون سایه
از کنار پاهایش روییده است.

پاییز ۱۳۴۰ در راه بروجرد

===machine===

In the furnace of the roads....
Blue, gray, black
The figure of a peasant with his long staff
White, black
I speak of the bull
With a heap of thorns, rain-swept
Black, black
I speak of his luck
That, like a shadow
has grown from his feet.

Autumn 1340 on the road to Borujerd

===lantern===

On the back roads —
blue, grey, black —
stands the figure of a peasant with his long staff,
white and black:
I mean his donkey,
loaded down with a ton of rain-beaten thorns,
black, black:
I mean his fortune,
which, like a shadow,
has grown up out of the sides of his feet.

Autumn 1340, on the road to Borujerd

